# Peer-to-Peer International Trade Model Based on Blockchain and Smart Contracts: Theory and Practice of BTLC

**Authors:** Junjie Yan, Wennan Wang, Duanyang Feng, Shiyang Song, Chengyifan Li

## Abstract
This study focuses on BTLC, a peer-to-peer international trade model based on blockchain and smart contracts, which aims to reform the traditional let- ter of credit process, improve international trade efficiency, reduce costs and improve security. By elaborating the BTLC model, this study demonstrates how blockchain technology as well as smart contract technology can be applied in the field of international trade to effectively solve the problems existing in the tra- ditional letter of credit process, such as high transaction costs due to too many intermediaries, high transaction risks due to an imperfect trust mechanism, and inefficiency in transactions. In addition, this paper further proves the superiority of the BTLC model in theory and practice through empirical research. It provides an in-depth discussion of the potential application and development direction of the model in future research. However, there are still some challenges and lim- itations in the practical application of the BTLC model. These challenges and limitations include the need for further empirical studies to validate the model's effectiveness and the problems faced. These include technical standards, laws and regulations. Therefore, this study suggests that future research directions should focus on the implementation challenges of blockchain technology, as well as the application of blockchain technology in other fields, in order to promote the wide application of blockchain technology in international trade.

